Theorem CN-8: Borrowed locality ceiling

  Preconditions:
    - s.access = Borrowed
    - s.locality > FunctionLocal (ArgEscaping, HeapEscaping, or Unknown)

  Soundness property:
    canonicalize_cn8(s).locality = FunctionLocal.

  Proof obligation:
    Finite enumeration over 1 Access (Borrowed) x 3 wide-locality variants
    = 3 trigger input states; verify CN-8 clamps all three to FunctionLocal.
    Negative enumeration: Borrowed + FunctionLocal preserves; Owned x any
    locality preserves (CN-8 does not fire on Owned).

    CN-8 monotonicity: forces locality DOWN (toward BlockLocal end of
    chain); non-monotone in standard max-join sense but monotone in
    canonicalization-as-feasibility-projection sense per Annex E §AIMS.8 L-7 idempotency.

    Engines dispatched:
      case_analysis (3-trigger + 6-negative locality enumeration per
        section_03::verify_cn8_borrowed_locality_ceiling)

  Expected:
    status: valid
    reason: section_03 case_analysis engine discharges CN-8 via 3-trigger + 6-negative locality enumeration
